  "agent_descriptions": [],
  "final": "`GET /files/<name>` now works. A signed-in user gets the file's contents back as `200` with `text/plain`. All 8 tests pass, including the 5 new ones.\n\n- **Auth:** with no valid token it returns `401`, same as the other routes.\n- **Other users' files:** a user can only read from their own folder. A request for a name that doesn't exist, or that belongs to someone else, gets `404`.\n- **Bad names:** the route reuses the name check from uploads, so `..`, names with `/` or `\\`, and leading-dot names are rejected with `404`. I also added a check for NUL bytes (`\\0`) in names, which the upload check had missed. That makes `POST /files` reject such names too.\n- **Response headers:** it sends `Content-Disposition: attachment` and `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`, so browsers download the file instead of rendering it. Without these, an uploaded HTML file could run script on your origin.\n\nThe route is in `files_app/app.py`, the file-reading helper is in `files_app/storage.py`, and the README lists the new route.",
